.TH "CLOSEWATCHER.CLOSE_EVENT" "3JS" "March 2, 2026" "JavaScript" "JavaScript Reference Manual"
.SH NAME
CloseWatcher.close_event \- CloseWatcher: close event
.SH SYNOPSIS
A \f[CR]close\f[R] event is fired at a \f[CR]CloseWatcher\f[R] object
when a close request was received and only fired if the
\f[CR]cancel\f[R] event that preceded the \f[CR]close\f[R] one was not
canceled.
.PP
The \f[CR]close\f[R] event handler is where the code to close the UI
component should be called: this ensures that the component will be
closed properly either from the platform\-specific close signal or from
a call to \f[CR]CloseWatcher.requestClose()\f[R].
.SH SYNTAX
Use the event name in methods like \f[CR]addEventListener()\f[R], or set
an event handler property.
.IP
.EX
addEventListener(\(dqclose\(dq, (event) => { })

onclose = (event) => { }
.EE
.SH EVENT TYPE
An \f[CR]Event\f[R].
.SH EXAMPLES
.SS Using the \f[CR]close\f[R] event
Use the \f[CR]close\f[R] to listen for close requests.
.IP
.EX
watcher.addEventListener(\(dqclose\(dq, () \f[B]=>\f[R] {
  \f[I]// Close your UI component\f[R]
  sidebar.hide();
});
.EE
